{"name":"Granite Brown","hex":"#3d2d24","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"granite","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A group of igneous and plutonic rocks composed primarily of feldspar and quartz. Usually contains one or more dark minerals, which may be mica, pyroxene, or amphibole. Granite is quarried for building stone, road gravel, decorative stone, and tombstones. Common colors are gray, white, pink, and yellow-brown.","Toughness; the quality of having a thick skin or being rough."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/granite"},{"term":"brown","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour like that of chocolate or coffee.","One of the colour balls used in snooker, with a value of 4 points."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a brown color/colour.","Gloomy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brown"}],"entries":[{"title":"Granite","blocks":[{"text":"Granite is a coarse-grained (phaneritic) intrusive igneous rock composed mostly of quartz, alkali feldspar, mica and plagioclase. It forms from magma with a high content of silica and alkali metal oxides that slowly cools and solidifies underground. It is common in the continental crust of Earth, where it is found in igneous intrusions. These range in size from dikes only a few centimeters across to batholiths exposed over hundreds of square kilometers."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Bianco_Sardo_Granit_mit_polierter_Oberfl%C3%A4che.jpg/330px-Bianco_Sardo_Granit_mit_polierter_Oberfl%C3%A4che.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Granite","wikidata":"Q41177"},{"title":"Brown","blocks":[{"text":"Brown is a color. It can be thought as a darker, typically desaturated shade of orange, and can often be produced by combining red and yellow with another color, namely blue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg/330px-Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brown","wikidata":"Q47071"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Granite_Rosa_Porri%C3%B1o_-_es_%28rotated%29.jpg/500px-Granite_Rosa_Porri%C3%B1o_-_es_%28rotated%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Granite_Rosa_Porri%C3%B1o_-_es_%28rotated%29.jpg/1280px-Granite_Rosa_Porri%C3%B1o_-_es_%28rotated%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Granite_Rosa_Porri%C3%B1o_-_es_%28rotated%29.jpg/500px-Granite_Rosa_Porri%C3%B1o_-_es_%28rotated%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGranite_Rosa_Porri%C3%B1o_-_es_(rotated).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Granite_BALMORAL.jpg/500px-Granite_BALMORAL.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Granite_BALMORAL.jpg/1280px-Granite_BALMORAL.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Granite_BALMORAL.jpg/500px-Granite_BALMORAL.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGranite_BALMORAL.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/%D0%93%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%BD%D0%B8%D1%82_%D0%BF%D0%BE%D0%B4_%D0%BC%D0%B8%D0%BA%D1%80%D0%BE%D1%81%D0%BA%D0%BE%D0%BF%D0%BE%D0%BC_2.jpg/500px-%D0%93%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%BD%D0%B8%D1%82_%D0%BF%D0%BE%D0%B4_%D0%BC%D0%B8%D0%BA%D1%80%D0%BE%D1%81%D0%BA%D0%BE%D0%BF%D0%BE%D0%B